# Source is authored and committed with LF. The CI matrix runs on
# windows-latest, where Git's default core.autocrlf=true rewrites every text
# file to CRLF on checkout. Doc/FUNCTION_INDEX.* and Doc/DOCUMENTATION_INDEX.*
# are keyed off a raw-byte sha256 of each source file (see
# scripts/utilities/generateFunctionIndex.mts), so that rewrite changed every
# hash on every Windows checkout and made the "generated docs drifted" gate
# fail regardless of whether anything had actually changed. Force LF on
# checkout so the byte content — and therefore the hash — matches what was
# committed.
* text=auto eol=lf
